    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but upskilling and shorter work weeks feel like band-aids when we're talking about actual mass unemployment from LLMs and robotics. if the robots are doing the work, the wealth just pools at the top. wouldnt you agree that without a mechanism like UBI to redistribute that wealth, the whole system just breaks down? it seems like the only logical path forward.",
